  "privacy.title": "Data and privacy", "privacy.lede": "Laverta receives visual reports and lets the newsroom publish a correction that can be viewed with a code. This page describes data used in the current prototype.", "privacy.section1": "Your account", "privacy.section1Text": "Account creation sends your email address, name and, if provided, newsroom to the Laverta server. Better Auth handles sign-in details and stores the account, password hash, sessions and temporary sign-in limits in PostgreSQL. Passwords are not stored in plain text. If SMTP is configured, it is used for confirmation and recovery links.", "privacy.section2": "Reports and images", "privacy.section2Text": "The form stores the claim, context, topic, language and post link you provide. The claim can be viewed with the LV code and by the newsroom. An attached image is encrypted and kept for up to 30 days. Its metadata may remain visible to the newsroom.", "privacy.section3": "Separate Gemini analysis", "privacy.section3Text": "Image verification is separate from the report form. An image in that workspace is sent to Gemini only after explicit consent. Do not share confidential or sensitive images, or images you do not have the right to use.", "privacy.section4": "Access and identity", "privacy.section4Text": "The form does not ask for a name, email or account. The LV code provides access to status and any published correction; keep it private. ‘No account’ does not guarantee network anonymity: the host may process technical logs.", "privacy.section5": "Services and security", "privacy.section5Text": "Accounts and reports are stored in the configured PostgreSQL database. The encryption key stays on the server; if lost, encrypted images cannot be recovered. Database encryption does not replace encryption of disks and backups.", "privacy.section6": "Messenger reports", "privacy.section6Text": "The Messenger bot stores in PostgreSQL the text of a confirmed report, its topic, where it was seen, the town or region given, the date, status, chosen language, a tracking code and the Page-scoped Messenger ID, used to reply and to follow up the report. Photos and files sent through Messenger are neither downloaded nor kept. An unconfirmed draft is deleted after 24 hours. These reports are not sent to Gemini, and the team export does not include the Messenger ID. How long they are kept must be decided before any public launch.", "privacy.demoTitle": "For the demo","privacy.demoText": "Use a public or authorised, non-sensitive image and a clearly marked exercise case. Results are leads for review: the editorial decision remains human.", "privacy.versionNote": "Prototype version · 2 November 2026. Before a public launch, review hosting logs, backups, rate limits, key rotation and data purge schedules.",
